libdtfl: timely and differential dataflow for C
================================================

libdtfl is a C11 library that brings the features of three Rust
projects to C programmers:

* timely dataflow, a data-parallel runtime for cyclic dataflows with
  partially ordered timestamps and progress tracking, on one thread,
  many threads, or many processes;
  https://github.com/TimelyDataflow/timely-dataflow

* differential dataflow, incrementally maintained collections
  (map, join, reduce, iterate, shared arrangements), its graph
  algorithms, and the dogsdogsdogs worst-case-optimal joins;
  https://github.com/TimelyDataflow/differential-dataflow

* the timely diagnostics tools, as an in-process WebSocket server and
  the dtfl-diag program.
  https://github.com/TimelyDataflow/diagnostics

Status: planning.  No code exists yet.  The design is in dev/PLAN.md,
the per-file port status is in dev/port-ledger.tsv, and the rules for
contributors (human or otherwise) are in AGENTS.md.

libdtfl is distributed under the MIT license; see COPYING, which also
carries the notices of the upstream projects it is derived from.
